start     book
terminals word

# What turns up in the world's chests and the lost library (design §4.2): short, flat, plainly attached, and
# from common words. It stokes curiosity rather than teaching structure, which is the advanced book's job.

# Modifiers lead, the page they modify closes the clause (design §4.3.1): "a desolate Age with packed ice
# landmass, frozen air" rather than "landmass packed_ice".

# One book in six is a rare material's onramp: nothing else says ahead of time what grows one, so these are
# how a player finds out. The rest are curiosities. LootBookCheck holds both halves -- every material book
# grows its material, and no curiosity grows any.

book = [curiosity_age]@5 | [rare_material_age]

rare_material_age =
  [arc_crystal_age]
  | [phasmium_age]
  | [rime_crystal_age]
  | [temperstone_age]
  | [astrite_age]

# Curiosity ages
# Meant to show what the mod can do and encourage experimentation without directly giving too much
# progression: a landmass worth looking at, and two or three things to look at in it. They never name a
# phenomenon kept for the materials and instability, nor a volcano, so no curiosity passes a gate.

# Between them the curiosities must use every aiming page at least once: a basic book is where a player
# first meets the parts of a world there are to aim at. The pages are landmass, sea, rock, underground,
# biomes, sky, structures, climate, surface, features, spawns, air, waters, weather, sun, moon, stars, grass,
# leaves, aurora, rainbow, phenomena and clouds. Surface, weather and moon came last, as a moon, a
# weather and a ground to stand on in what there is to look at.

# One thing to look at and one thing to find, each drawn from its own group so no two say the same part of
# the world twice -- two leaf colours, or a tropical and an arid climate, is a book arguing with itself. A
# climate is only ever the third, and never beside a mood, which leans the climate its own way.
# What there is to look at is overhead, so only a landmass open to the sky gets one: an aurora in a roofed
# world is a page nobody can see.
curiosity_age =
    [mood] age [open_curious_landmass] [look_beside_a_mood]
    | [mood] age [curious_landmass] [thing]
    | age [open_curious_landmass] [look] [thing]@4
    | age [open_curious_landmass] [look] [landed_thing] [mild_climate]@2
    | age [open_curious_landmass] [bare_look] [bare_thing] [barren_climate]
    | age [curious_landmass] [thing_beside_a_sea] [sea]
    | [palm_beach_age]

# The palm beach: a ribbon rather than a trophy (Jonah, 2026-09-30), so it is a curiosity and common ink. An
# island, so there is a beach for it, and warmth or something to look at beside it -- it grows only where
# the coast is mild, and a book that named it on a cold Age would be a page that did nothing.
palm_beach_age =
    age [palm_landmass] landmass palm_beach biomes [palm_climate]@2
    | age [palm_landmass] landmass [look] palm_beach biomes

palm_landmass = insular@3 | archipelagic@3 | [size] insular

palm_climate = tropical climate | warm climate

curious_landmass = [typical_landmass] landmass@3 | [size] [typical_landmass] landmass@2 | [stone] [typical_landmass] landmass

open_curious_landmass = [open_landmass] landmass@3 | [size] [open_landmass] landmass@2 | [stone] [open_landmass] landmass

look = [sky]@4 | [aurora]@2 | [rainbow]@2 | [ground]@2 | [moon] | [weather]

# Beside a mood, no moon: `moonless` is one.
look_beside_a_mood = [sky]@4 | [aurora]@2 | [rainbow]@2 | [ground]@2 | [weather]

thing = [landed_thing]@4 | [sea]

# Without the sea, for beside a climate: a drowned sea and an arid climate are watery against dry.
landed_thing = [formation]@3 | [underground]@3 | [life]@2

# And without dry rock, for beside a sea: `dry rock` and `drowned sea` are dry against watery, which
# BookCheck caught at seed 341 once the palm beach's shape moved which book each seed draws.
# And without a settlement, for beside a sea: `settled structures` and `open sea` are inhabited against empty.
thing_beside_a_sea = [formation]@3 | [underground_beside_a_sea]@3 | [life_beside_a_sea]@2

# A barren climate only beside what does not live or grow: herds and trees are grazing and wooded against
# barren (the antonym pairs of 2026-10-04, which made one basic book in four hundred unstable).
bare_look = [sky]@4 | [aurora]@2 | [rainbow]@2 | [moon]

bare_thing = [formation]@3 | [underground]@3 | ruins structures | untouched structures

underground_beside_a_sea =
    tunnels underground@4
    | fissured underground@4
    | chambered underground@3
    | riddled rock@3
    | [size] tunnels underground@2
    | delved underground
    | hollow underground
    | lattice underground

# Arc crystals: a tempest, and an aurora most nights and fierce.
arc_crystal_age =
    age [arc_crystal_landmasses] landmass [tempest_options] [aurora_options]
    | age [arc_crystal_landmasses] landmass [tempest_options] [aurora_options] [flavour]@2

# Open to the sky: a roofed world has no curtains to stand in it.
arc_crystal_landmasses = [open_landmass]@3 | skyborne | end | tangled

tempest_options = tempest phenomena@3 | teeming tempest phenomena

# Described rather than named: a curtain with anything said of it is one, and this says it comes every
# night and burns bright, which is the gate's half.
aurora_options =
    restless glimmering aurora@3
    | restless glimmering [aurora_colour] aurora@2
    | restless glimmering colossal aurora

# Phasmium: a water sea raised to an abyss, and a deluge. The shapes whose seas are broad and flat-floored,
# since those are where the abyss grows.
phasmium_age =
    age [phasmium_landmasses] landmass deep water sea deluge phenomena
    | age [phasmium_landmasses] landmass deep water sea deluge phenomena [flavour]@2

phasmium_landmasses = insular@3 | archipelagic@3 | eroded@2 | sheer@2 | continental | gentle | pillared

# Rime crystal: cold enough that nothing thaws, and a blizzard. The cold is said to the climate, since
# `blizzard phenomena` keeps the blizzard's own cold on the phenomena.
rime_crystal_age =
    age [rime_crystal_landmasses] landmass [cold] blizzard phenomena
    | age [rime_crystal_landmasses] landmass [cold] blizzard phenomena [flavour]@2

# Sheer ground first: rime is won by climbing, and ramps with height.
rime_crystal_landmasses = [typical_landmass]@3 | mountainous@2 | sheer@2 | pillared | cleft | shattered

cold = frozen climate

# Temperstone: every climate as hot as a desert, and volcanoes. `volcanic` admits the volcano by name, which
# the gate reads; a lava sea is drawn beside it now and then, and pays nothing alone.
temperstone_age =
    age [seaworthy_landmass] landmass scorching climate volcanic features
    | age [seaworthy_landmass] landmass scorching climate lava sea volcanic features
    | age [seaworthy_landmass] landmass scorching climate volcanic features [flavour]@2

# Astrite: meteors. Cratered country and a dark night are drawn beside it, since that is what it looks like.
astrite_age =
    age [astrite_landmasses] landmass meteors phenomena
    | age [astrite_landmasses] landmass meteors phenomena [night]@2
    | moonless age [astrite_landmasses] landmass meteors phenomena
    | age [astrite_landmasses] landmass meteors phenomena [flavour]@2

astrite_landmasses = [open_landmass]@3 | cratered@3 | flat | pyramidal

night = bright stars | glimmering stars | [sky_colour] sky

# Reusable components

typical_landmass = [standard_landmasses]@10 | [uncommon_landmasses]@5 | [exotic_landmasses]

standard_landmasses =
    overworld
    | continental
    | archipelagic
    | canyoned
    | eroded
    | gentle
    | insular
    | mountainous
    | riverine

uncommon_landmasses =
    cleft
    | cratered
    | nether
    | pillared
    | shattered
    | sheer
    | subterranean

exotic_landmasses =
    end
    | flat
    | pyramidal
    | skyborne
    | tangled

# A sea to be poured: nothing hanging in the void, nothing with no waterline, and none of vanilla's own
# rock, which brings its own sea and would not take ours.
seaworthy_landmass =
    continental@3
    | archipelagic@3
    | canyoned@2
    | eroded@2
    | gentle@3
    | insular@3
    | mountainous@2
    | riverine@2
    | cleft
    | cratered
    | pillared
    | shattered
    | sheer

# Open to the sky, for what falls out of it.
open_landmass =
    [standard_landmasses]@10
    | cleft@2
    | cratered@2
    | pillared@2
    | shattered@2
    | sheer@2
    | end
    | flat
    | pyramidal
    | skyborne
    | tangled

# What a material book may carry beside its gate: nothing that touches a climate, a sea or a phenomenon,
# which are the things a gate is made of.
flavour = [sky]@4 | [formation]@3 | [underground]@2 | [ground] | [life]

# Said of the whole Age, so written before its page.
# Evocative only: a narrowing word here (`uncanny` narrows the landmass) fractures against the one named.
# And none that leans towards a phenomenon a gate is made of: broad words reach every phenomenon, so
# `savage` (hostile) draws meteors and tempests and `beautiful` (bright) meteors, and a curiosity must not
# pass a gate. `foreboding` leans hostile too.
mood = wondrous | ancient | looming | desolate | pristine | homely | moonless

size = minuscule | small | large | colossal

stone = blackstone | calcite | deepslate | tuff | sandstone | red_sandstone | andesite | granite | diorite

colour = red | orange | yellow | green | cyan | blue | indigo | purple | magenta | black | white | grey

sky_colour = [colour]

aurora_colour = green@3 | blue@2 | purple@2 | red | white

# The sky: its colour, its bodies, and what hangs in the air under it.
sky =
    [sky_colour] sky@3
    | [colour] sun@2
    | colossal sun
    | small sun
    | [colour] sun [colour] sun
    | [rising] sun
    | [colour] clouds
    | overcast sky
    | bright stars
    | glimmering stars
    | [colour] air@2
    | inky air
    | clear air

# A colour is not said of a moon; its size and where it rises are.
moon = colossal moon | small moon | [rising] moon

# Wet weather only, and never beside a barren climate: drenched is watery against dry. `parched` is a
# climate's word as much as the weather's, so it is left to the climates.
weather = drenched weather | stormy weather

rising = rising_east | rising_north | rising_northeast | rising_northwest | rising_south | rising_southeast | rising_southwest | rising_west

# A curtain is had by describing it. Never both restless and glimmering here, which with a tempest drawn in
# by a mood would be the arc crystal's gate.
aurora =
    [aurora_colour] aurora@3
    | restless aurora
    | glimmering [aurora_colour] aurora
    | colossal [aurora_colour] aurora

rainbow =
    rainbows phenomena@2
    | rainbows phenomena [colour] rainbow
    | rainbows phenomena colossal rainbow
    | rainbows phenomena prismatic rainbow

formation = [formation_shape] features@2 | [stone] [formation_shape] features@2 | [size] [formation_shape] features

formation_shape = arches | boulders | obelisks | pyramids | rings | spikes

# The dramatic undergrounds are the rare end of this: halls, the hollow and the lattice.
underground =
    tunnels underground@4
    | fissured underground@4
    | chambered underground@3
    | riddled rock@3
    | dry rock
    | [size] tunnels underground@2
    | delved underground
    | hollow underground
    | lattice underground

# The ground and what grows on it, which is mostly colour.
ground = [colour] grass@2 | [colour] leaves@2 | [colour] grass [colour] leaves | flowers features | trees features | [surface_block] surface

# What the ground is laid with where grass would be.
surface_block = sand | red_sand | moss_block | podzol | mud | gravel | calcite | mycelium | snow_block

sea = drowned sea@2 | open sea | shallow water sea | murky waters | clear waters | [colour] waters

life = teeming herds spawns | fish spawns | fliers spawns | beasts spawns | ruins structures | settled structures | untouched structures

life_beside_a_sea = teeming herds spawns | fish spawns | fliers spawns | beasts spawns | ruins structures | untouched structures

mild_climate = temperate climate@2 | warm climate | tropical climate | verdant biomes

barren_climate = parched climate | arid climate
